      "_horizon_note": "REVERTED to 12 on 2026-08-20, and the reason is worth recording. Gate A refused N=12 (discarded tail 2.0% of value, decay factor 0.900) and its message says to extend the horizon. Extending to 20 was tried and MADE IT WORSE: the tail rose to 4.1% of value at a factor of 0.915. The gate's own remedy does not work for this scenario, because the discarded tail is contrib[N] x d/(1-d) and contrib carries an annuity factor that grows with N faster than the per-year decay shrinks it. There is no horizon at which this bear path spends its abnormal growth: revenue at 1.6% with flat margins and NOA growth at 1.6% leaves the return on net operating assets above the cost of capital forever, so the forecast asserts a permanent advantage. That is a statement about the DRIVERS, not the horizon, and changing them would be writing James's bear case for him. Cleared instead with convergence.reviewed in PEP.yaml."
